# gui_health_demo — a real Win32 GUI runtime check (WS3-044). Binds the
# SemanticScript Win32 GUI runtime (sem_win32_gui_runtime.c) through the
# eav_gui_health_check seam: it creates a real window with an auto-close handler,
# runs the Win32 message loop, and tears down — returning 0. (On a desktop the
# window flashes briefly; with no interactive desktop the runtime reports
# unavailable, which the check maps to 0.) Kept out of examples/ so run_examples
# never flashes a window; test_gui.py runs it and asserts status 0.

GuiHealthDemo is project
GuiHealthDemo module fix
GuiHealthDemo target console
GuiHealthDemo entry main

fix is module
fix path fix.mod
fix exports main
fix purpose "Host the GUI health-check entry"
fix invariant "Exposes main, which runs the Win32 GUI health check and returns its status"

guiHealthCheck is operation
guiHealthCheck out Int32
guiHealthCheck body runtimeBinding eav_gui_health_check
guiHealthCheck purpose "Create a window, auto-close it, and return the GUI runtime status (0 = ok)"
guiHealthCheck suppress SS5000 because "GUI runtime seam; the typed home is std/standard.gui.sem"

main is operation
main out Int32
main async no
main purpose "Run the Win32 GUI health check and exit with its status"
main invariant "Exit 0 means the GUI runtime created + ran + closed a window (or is headless-unavailable)"
main do checkCall
main return status

checkCall is call
checkCall in main
checkCall invokes guiHealthCheck
checkCall out status Int32
